The unexported spelling is the alias this time: inner aliases the exported Visible, and
the rendered type mentions Visible first. Rendering names the alias, so lib.inner is
unreachable from the destination even though its target is exported, and the exported
target being walked first must not mark the alias as already seen.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrUnreachableType
-- example.com/lib/lib.go --
package lib

type Visible struct{ X int }
type inner = Visible
type Thing struct{}

//plumb:build
func New(m map[Visible]inner) *Thing { return &Thing{} }
